WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.335
"Why Do Milk Drinkers Live
Shorter Lives on Average?"

00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:09.360
In my video
on milk and bones,

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.880
I discussed
this set of studies,

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.640
following a hundred thousand
people for up to two decades,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.120
finding a 60% higher risk
of hip fracture

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.560
among women who drank
a lot of milk.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.000
The researchers suggested it
might be due to the galactose,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.820
which is a breakdown product
of the milk sugar lactose,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.940
based on the fact that people
with high levels in their blood,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.180
because they were born with an
inability to detoxify the stuff,

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.980
can end up
with weakened bones.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.160
But that's not all
galactose can do.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.580
Galactose is what scientists use

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.880
to cause accelerated aging
in lab animals,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.120
since it's so successful
at mimicking aging

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.820
by inducing degenerative changes
in the brain,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:53.280
heart, lungs, liver,
kidney, etc.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:56.760
"Life-shortened animals
showed neurodegeneration,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.280
mental retardation,
and cognitive dysfunction,

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.080
diminished immune responses

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.120
and a reduction
of reproductive ability."

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.280
And it doesn't take much,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:06.900
just the human equivalent

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.120
of one to two glasses worth
of milk a day.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.320
However, humans aren't rodents.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.480
For example, we've known
for nearly a century

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.940
that you can cause cataracts
in rats

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.760
by feeding them lots
of lactose or galactose,

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:23.760
but the epidemiological data
is mixed

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.340
as to whether dairy
is doing the same in people.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.760
The Swedish studies didn't
just look at bone, though,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.680
but milk and mortality.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:35.520
More milk was associated
with more death.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.980
In women,
three glasses of milk a day

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:41.220
was associated with nearly twice
the risk of dying prematurely.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:43.500
The medical journal editorial

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.440
accompanying the study
emphasized that,

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:47.880
given the rise
in milk consumption

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:48.540
around the world,

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.060
the "role of milk in mortality

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:54.000
needs to be established
definitively now."

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.260
With the then-largest-ever study
on milk intake and mortality

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.180
suggesting such adverse effects,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.020
Harvard researchers stepped in
with three of their cohorts

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.240
to form a study twice as big

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.700
to see if the earlier findings
were just a fluke.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.880
Following more than
200,000 men and women

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.020
for up to three decades,

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.960
they confirmed the bad news.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.000
Those who consumed more dairy

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.980
lived significantly shorter
lives.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.740
Every half serving more
of regular milk a day

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.580
was associated with
9% increased risk of dying

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.140
from cardiovascular disease,

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.480
11% increased risk
of dying from cancer,

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.700
and an 11% increased risk
of dying

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.140
from all causes put together.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.960
This is all the more remarkable

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.360
since milk drinking
is typically associated

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.560
with healthier habits,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.440
like more exercise
and less smoking and drinking,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:46.140
though they did try to control
for all these factors.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.560
Of course it does matter
what you eat instead.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.780
This Harvard analysis published

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.980
in the New England Journal
of Medicine,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.080
found that swapping dairy
for meat,

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.940
red meat, poultry, or fish,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.960
would not be expected
to do your body any favors,

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.860
and you would be expected
to live longer eating dairy

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.500
than eggs or processed meat.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.120
It's only when you swap dairy

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.040
for plant-based sources
of protein

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.980
did they find a significant drop
in mortality risk.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.160
When all of the milk
and mortality studies

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:17.640
are put together,

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.100
it appears
the excess mortality risk

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.400
is limited to regular as opposed
to low-fat, like skim milk.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.300
This suggests it may be more
of a saturated fat issue,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.620
though that doesn't explain why
soured, or fermented milk

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.060
appears to have
the opposite impact.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.360
So maybe it's both the butterfat
and the galactose.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.600
A randomized crossover study
of low-fat dairy,

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.000
fermented dairy,
and unfermented dairy

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.680
found that study subjects

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.440
had significantly higher
IL-6 inflammation levels

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.140
during unfermented
regular dairy weeks

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.000
compared to when they were
switched to either

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.180
the fermented
or low-fat dairy products.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.200
The fermentation process can
eliminate some of the galactose.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.180
As we age, our ability
to detoxify galactose

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.340
declines by as much as 40%,

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.740
which would make it
even more important

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.480
to avoid dairy later in life

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.820
if indeed galactose
is the culprit.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.940
But if galactose
does its dirty work

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.040
through oxidation
and inflammation,

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.620
might increased fruit
and vegetable intake

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.180
help mediate some of the harm?

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.720
In animals,
galactose-induced aging

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.060
can be slowed by fruit
and vegetable consumption.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.700
For example,
feeding rats blueberries

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:33.420
can decrease the brain damage
induced by the milk sugar.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.940
Might it be able to help

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.980
with the higher levels
of oxidative stress

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.440
and inflammation found
among human milk drinkers?

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:44.040
Unfortunately, women drinking
three or more glasses of milk

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.260
a day had more than twice
the risk of hip fractures

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.420
compared to women drinking
less than a glass a day

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:52.560
regardless of whether
they were eating more, or less,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.700
fruits and vegetables.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.720
But, those high milk consumers

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.020
consuming five or more servings
of fruits and vegetables a day

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.540
did reduce their chance
of dying prematurely

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:07.140
to just 60% greater
than those drinking less milk,

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.940
so antioxidant rich foods

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:11.580
may be able to modify
the elevated death rate

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.040
associated with
high milk consumption.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.400
Highly influential
advocacy organizations,

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:20.640
such as the US National
Osteoporosis Foundation

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.020
or the Europe-based

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.060
International
Osteoporosis Foundation,

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.900
continue to push dairy, drugs,
and calcium supplements,

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:31.320
despite the countervailing
evidence that I've reviewed.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.280
Why do they keep pushing dairy,
drugs, and supplements?

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.700
Perhaps because their
objectivity is compromised

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.160
by the influence
of their commercial sponsors

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.040
that include companies
that market, you guessed it,

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.080
dairy, drugs,
and supplements.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:49.620
Most recent reviews
on dairy and osteoporosis

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.360
in the English-language
medical literature

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:52.260
were found to be written

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.080
by those with ties
to the dairy industry.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:58.680
The primary justification
for inclusion of dairy

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.240
in federal nutrition
recommendations

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:02.580
is based on
purported bone benefits

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.640
that are not supported
by the available evidence.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:09.180
What if dietary guidelines
were fashioned

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.400
without commercial influence?

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.860
In 2019, Canada decided
to exclude industry reports

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.060
and stick to the science

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.160
in the formation
of their new dietary guidelines.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.480
What a concept.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:24.300
Major changes
include the new emphasis

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.760
on plant-based food intake,
limiting junk,

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.240
and...the removal
of the dairy food group.

